[0.005, "o", "\u001b[4;35mGoal\u001b[0m                                                                                                  \r\n\r\nAdd the read-only \u001b[1;36;40mvalidate_tool_bundle\u001b[0m method to \u001b[1;36;40m@alvagante/content-tool\u001b[0m and use the mirrored         \r\nvalidators as one publication gate for an owner bundle.                                               \r\n\r\n\u001b[4;35mRead first\u001b[0m                                                                                            \r\n\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mdocs/plans/tool-bundle-plan.md\u001b[0m, Slice 1 and Decisions carried into the slices                      \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mdocs/adr/0054-tool-footprint-is-saidata-with-inline-evidence.md\u001b[0m                                    \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mdocs/adr/0055-scenarios-are-the-single-source-of-published-commands.md\u001b[0m                             \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mdata/tools.yaml\u001b[0m, \u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/content_tool.ts\u001b[0m, \u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/content_course.ts\u001b[0m, and       \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0m\u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[1;36;40m~/agents-docs/code-changes.md\u001b[0m                                                                      \r\n\r\n\u001b[4;35mFiles\u001b[0m                                                                                                 \r\n\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/content_tool.ts\u001b[0m and focused Deno tests                                           \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/content_course.ts\u001b[0m only if owner checks require its existing helpers              \r\n\r\n\u001b[4;35mAcceptance\u001b[0m                                                                                            \r\n\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mThe method resolves Tool IDs through the registry, checks published owner course and taught        \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mversion, validates saidata, usage and every Tool Scenario, and checks cross-file Scenario          \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mreferences and Target coverage. It works before \u001b[1;36;40mcontent.tool\u001b[0m is set so the flag can be settled     \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mafter validation.                                    "]
[0.000, "o", "                                              \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mValidation rejects missing files, invalid Evidence, duplicate or dangling references, and claims of\r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mverification unsupported by passing Scenario Evidence. It writes no bundle files and never reads   \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mHOWTO Scenario bodies into a Tool result.                                                          \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mLegacy \u001b[1;36;40m17\u001b[0m/\u001b[1;36;40m18\u001b[0m/\u001b[1;36;40m19\u001b[0m files remain until each Tool's bundle actually validates; this fragment does not   \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mdelete them.                                                                                       \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0mFollow the \u001b[1;36;40mtdd\u001b[0m and \u001b[1;36;40mswamp\u001b[0m skills for code and method invocation. Run focused Deno and site tests,   \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mapplicable type checks, the method on draft pilots, and \u001b[1;36;40mgit diff --check\u001b[0m.                          \r\n\r\n\u001b[4;35mNotes\u001b[0m                                                                                    "]
[0.000, "o", "             \r\n\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m2026-09-26T01:05:17+00:00: review by codex asked for changes: Reviewed \u001b[1;36;40mtools...HEAD\u001b[0m against the    \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mTool bundle plan and ADRs 0054 and 0055. The review fragment provides no explicit Acceptance       \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mcommands.                                                                                          \r\n\r\nChecks: \u001b[1;36;40mdeno test -A extensions/models/content_tool_bundle_test.ts\u001b[0m (10 passed); \u001b[1;36;40mdeno test -A \u001b[0m         \r\n\u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/content_tool*_test.ts extensions/models/saidata_validation_test.ts \u001b[0m                 \r\n\u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/tool_scenarios_test.ts\u001b[0m (46 passed); \u001b[1;36;40mdeno check extensions/models/content_tool.ts \u001b[0m   \r\n\u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/content_tool_bundle_test.ts\u001b[0m (passed); \u001b[1;36;40mpnpm typecheck\u001b[0m (passed); \u001b[1;36;40mgit diff --check \u001b[0m    \r\n\u001b[1;36;40mtools...HEAD\u001b[0m (passed).                                                                                \r\n\r\nBlock"]
[0.000, "o", "ing findings:                                                                                    \r\n\r\n\u001b[36m 1 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/content_tool.ts:902-930\u001b[0m: The gate checks only that a recipe's Scenario ID exists \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mand has a \u001b[1;36;40mpassed: true\u001b[0m file. It never compares \u001b[1;36;40musage.yaml\u001b[0m recipe commands or target overrides with \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mScenario steps. Changing a published recipe command after its Scenario ran still produces a        \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0msuccessful validation, contrary to ADR 0055's rule that the published command is exactly what ran. \r\n\u001b[36m 2 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/content_tool.ts:909-920\u001b[0m: The gate visits Evidence only when present. It accepts a\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0msaidata record with commands, settings, or other publishable facts that have no inline Evidence.   \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mADR 0054 explicitly prohibits publishing seeded values until Evidence backs them. The passing      \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mfixture itself has only one evidenced command, so the test suite"]
[0.000, "o", " does not cover this gap.          \r\n\u001b[36m 3 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/content_tool.ts:82-90,774-820\u001b[0m: A passing Evidence file contains only a Scenario  \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mID, \u001b[1;36;40mpassed\u001b[0m, timestamp, and runner; it has no Scenario content digest, step results, or version     \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mbinding. The gate therefore accepts an old pass after a Scenario's commands or assertions change.  \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mAs a publication gate, it cannot establish that the current Scenario actually ran successfully.    \r\n\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m2026-09-26T02:05:17+00:00: review by codex asked for changes: Reviewed \u001b[1;36;40mtools...HEAD\u001b[0m against the    \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mTool bundle plan and ADRs 0054 and 0055. The fragment specifies no Acceptance commands or Read     \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mfirst files. No code or plan files were edited.                                                    \r\n\r\nChecks:                                                                                               \r\n\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mdeno test --allow-read"]
[0.000, "o", " --allow-write --allow-env extensions/models/content_tool_bundle_test.ts\u001b[0m: 13 \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mpassed, 0 failed. The narrower runs without full environment access failed because the YAML        \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mdependency reads \u001b[1;36;40mLOG_TOKENS\u001b[0m and \u001b[1;36;40mLOG_STREAM\u001b[0m.                                                        \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mdeno check extensions/models/content_tool.ts extensions/models/content_tool_bundle_test.ts\u001b[0m: passed.\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mdeno lint extensions/models/content_tool_bundle_test.ts\u001b[0m: failed, 1 \u001b[1;36;40mrequire-await\u001b[0m error at line 225.\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mdeno lint extensions/models/content_tool.ts extensions/models/content_tool_bundle_test.ts\u001b[0m: failed, \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0m6 errors, including the new test error and existing errors in \u001b[1;36;40mcontent_tool.ts\u001b[0m.                     \r\n\r\nBlocking findings:                                                                                    \r\n\r\n\u001b[36m 1 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/content_tool.ts:8"]
[0.000, "o", "03-852\u001b[0m: The publication gate requires Evidence only on selected \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mtop-level lists, licenses and four provider lists. It accepts publishable facts without Evidence   \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0munder \u001b[1;36;40mproviders.*.packages\u001b[0m, \u001b[1;36;40mproviders.*.services\u001b[0m, \u001b[1;36;40mproviders.*.files\u001b[0m, \u001b[1;36;40mproviders.*.commands\u001b[0m,         \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mproviders.*.settings\u001b[0m, and nested command flags or subcommands. The saidata schema permits these    \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mnodes, so a complete bundle can validate while violating ADR 0054's per-record Evidence rule.      \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mTraverse all publishable saidata nodes and test a nested and provider fact with missing Evidence.  \r\n\u001b[36m 2 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/content_tool.ts:1022-1042\u001b[0m: A Lab reference is checked for existence and a passing\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mScenario, but never for its variant's Target. A Docker Lab can reference a Linux Scenario and still\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mvalidate. Require the referenced Scenario steps to cover the Lab va"]
[0.000, "o", "riant's Target, and test a      \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mmismatched variant.                                                                                \r\n\u001b[36m 3 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/content_tool_bundle_test.ts:225\u001b[0m: The added async \u001b[1;36;40mwriteResource\u001b[0m stub has no \u001b[1;36;40mawait\u001b[0m,\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mand \u001b[1;36;40mdeno lint\u001b[0m reports \u001b[1;36;40mrequire-await\u001b[0m. Fix the new lint failure before this change is accepted.      \r\n\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m2026-09-26T03:05:17+00:00: review by codex asked for changes: Reviewed \u001b[1;36;40mtools...HEAD\u001b[0m against the    \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mTool bundle plan and ADRs 0054 and 0055. The review fragment contains no explicit Acceptance       \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mcommands.                                                                                          \r\n\r\nCommands and results:                                                                                 \r\n\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mgit diff tools...HEAD --check\u001b[0m: passed.                                                      "]
[0.000, "o", "       \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mdeno test --allow-all extensions/models/content_tool_bundle_test.ts\u001b[0m: 16 passed, 0 failed.          \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mdeno test --allow-all extensions/models/content_tool_test.ts \u001b[0m                                      \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/tool_scenarios_test.ts extensions/models/tool_usage_test.ts \u001b[0m                     \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/saidata_validation_test.ts\u001b[0m: 38 passed, 0 failed.                                 \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mdeno check extensions/models/content_tool.ts extensions/models/content_tool_bundle_test.ts\u001b[0m: passed.\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mdeno lint extensions/models/content_tool.ts extensions/models/content_tool_bundle_test.ts\u001b[0m: failed  \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mwith five errors on unchanged lines of \u001b[1;36;40mcontent_tool.ts\u001b[0m (two import prefixes, two \u001b[1;36;40mrequire-await\u001b[0m, one\r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0munused argument).                                                                                  \r"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n\r\nBlocking findings:                                                                                    \r\n\r\n\u001b[36m 1 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/content_tool.ts:838\u001b[0m: The publication gate requires Evidence for fact arrays, but \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mskips publishable metadata and provider fields. For example, \u001b[1;36;40mmetadata.identifiers.purl\u001b[0m,            \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mmetadata.urls.website\u001b[0m, and \u001b[1;36;40mproviders.apt.prerequisites\u001b[0m can be populated with no Evidence and still \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mpass. The saidata draft schema allows Evidence on those nodes, and ADR 0054 requires published     \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mvalues to be backed by Evidence. Validate every publishable node before issuing                    \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mtool_bundle_validation\u001b[0m.                                                                            \r\n\u001b[36m 2 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40mextensions/models/content_tool.ts:928\u001b[0m: \u001b[1;36;40mscenario_step\u001b[0m Evidence is accepted when its \u001b[1;36;40msource\u001b[0m names any\r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0"]
[0.000, "o", "mpassing Scenario, even if \u001b[1;36;40mstep\u001b[0m names no executed step. The code also does not compare the inline   \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mrunner, image digest, architecture, or version to that Scenario's execution Evidence. Thus a fact  \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mcan claim execution provenance that the passing Scenario did not establish. Bind each inline claim \r\n\u001b[36m   \u001b[0mto an actual passing step and its matching execution metadata.                                     \r\n\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m2026-09-26T05:21:00+00:00: operator retry: Last round. Close the gate with one rule the review can \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mcheck, instead of an enumeration: (1) every publishable node in saidata.yaml (including            \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mmetadata.identifiers, metadata.urls and provider fields) needs Evidence, except an explicit        \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mallowlist written in the code as a named constant, with one comment line per entry saying why; (2) \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mscenario_step Evidence must name a step that exists in a passing Scenario, and its runner and image\r\n\u001b[1m "]
[0.000, "o", "  \u001b[0mdigest must match that Scenario's recorded run. Add a test for each. Fix only these two round 3    \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mfindings. Anything else a reviewer raises is a follow-up, not a blocker: the loopq review template \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mnow says so. The five deno lint errors on unchanged lines of content_tool.ts are handled by        \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mtb-0076; do not touch them here.                                                                   \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m2026-09-26T06:11:22+00:00: integrated into tools at d0f19f9dc88d                                   \r\n"]
